p APIs.\n- The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props (styles go in `sx`), and `slotProps.primary` for ListItemText, `slotProps.paper` for Popover and `slotProps.input` for Switch.\n- The admin email log reuses the shared DataTable as planned. DataTable's built-in search box writes `?q=`, which the email-log API ignores, so search has no effect there. Making it work would need a DataTable or API change outside this ticket's scope.\n- shell.tsx still has two lint errors (`Avatar` and `theme` unused). They were already there before this change and are not touched.\n- TASK-18: Seed demo notifications — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Unit tests (notifications) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Integration tests (dispatch) + vitest include — ✓ complete\n\nVerification for TASK-18 to TASK-20:\n- Seed:\n  - With the users missing, it logs a skip for each email.\n  - With temporary student@ and parent@ users, two seed runs leave exactly 3 rows each (1 read). The temporary users were removed afterwards.\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: 28 tests pass.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`:\n  - With `TEST_DATABASE_URL` pointing at the local DB, all 3 tests pass: concurrent dispatch sends each row once, a row stuck in SENDING for 11 minutes goes back to PENDING with attempts unchanged, and a freshly claimed SENDING row is left alone.\n  - Without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`, the tests are skipped.\n- Full `vitest run`: 112 tests pass. Three files fail, and none of them import code changed in this ticket:\n  - `lockout.test.ts`: next-auth cannot resolve `next/server` under vitest.\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx`: the `@mui/x-internals` exports map.\n  - `useToast.test.tsx`: the auto-hide timer test.\n- TASK-21: Playwright e2e (bell + preferences) — ✓ complete\n\n### HTTP verification (next dev on :3100, temporary admin, all data removed afterwards)\n- Without a session, `/api/notifications/unread-count` returns 401. Credentials sign-in works.\n- Notification flow:\n  - The admin test button returns `{ok:true}` and the unread count goes from 0 to 1.\n  - The list `category=SYSTEM` filter returns the row; ACADEMIC returns nothing; a bad category returns 400.\n  - read/unread toggles the count. Another user's id returns 404. read-all returns `{count:1}`, then the count is 0.\n- Preferences:\n  - GET returns only `system.test`; the emailOnly types are hidden.\n  - PUT persists the change.\n  - PUT returns VALIDATION_ERROR for `account.invite`, for `__proto__`, and for an extra key.\n- Email log:\n  - The `status` filter works and the response has no html or text.\n  - Retry on a non-FAILED row returns 404; retry on a FAILED row resets it to PENDING.\n- Dispatch:\n  - No token or a wrong token returns 401.\n  - The correct bearer token returns `{sent:1}`.\n- Pages:\n  - `/notifications` and `/account/notifications` render (200).\n  - The SSR markup has `role=\"switch\"` with the label \"Test notification email\" and the bell's \"Notifications\" label, matching the e2e selectors.\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA\n1. **Pre-existing dependency mismatch breaks every DataGrid page.**\n   - Cause: `package-lock.json` resolves `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` against `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0`, so `./useFirstRender` is not exported.\n   - Effect: `/admin/email-log` (TASK-17) returns 500, and so does the existing `/admin/sections`. It is also why `DataTable.test.tsx` fails.\n   - Not fixed here, because the plan keeps `package.json` untouched.\n   - Fix: align the MUI X versions (for example, install `@mui/x-internals` at the version matching data-grid 9.5.0). After that, the first e2e test can pass, since it starts on `/admin/email-log`.\n2. **The e2e spec was not executed.**\n   - Cause: `@playwright/test@1.47.2` needs chromium revision 1248, but only 1200 is installed locally.\n   - It is listed by `playwright test --list` and its flow was exercised over HTTP as described above.\n   - To run it: `npx playwright install chromium`, then `npm run test:e2e`.\n3. The integration tests need `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. They pass against the local DB on :5433.\n4. The worker and cron route require env to be loaded. tsx does not read `.env` for `env.ts`. The worker happened to work locally because PrismaClient loads `.env` first. In production, set the variables in the process environment.\n----\n# QA Report — SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-6\n- timestamp: 2026-11-05T10:36:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 61\n- requirementsPassed: 34\n- requirementsFailed: 27 (1 FAIL + 26 NOT-IMPLEMENTED)\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **Dev stopped after TASK-8. The whole UI and the seed are missing.**\n   - Not built: TASK-9 to TASK-16, which cover the grid, the bell schedule page, the timetable editor, the personal, student and course timetable views, navigation, the seed, and the e2e test.\n   - None of the 25 planned CREATE files for those tasks exist.\n   - The planned edits to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `shell.tsx` and `seed.ts` were not made.\n   - `@dnd-kit/core` was added to `package.json` but is never imported.\n2. **The Dev artifacts are stale and do not describe this ticket.**\n   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 (Notifications) files dated 2026-11-04. Their \"TASK-1..21 complete\" claims refer to PRD-04.\n   - No SH-6 dev log exists, but `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`. The pipeline accepted a Dev phase that never wrote its own outputs.\n3. **The backend that does exist is solid.**\n   - Covers TASK-1 to TASK-8: schema, migration, validators, clash engine, service, and 10 API routes.\n   - Contains real logic, with no stubs, TODO markers or console.log calls.\n   - Typecheck and lint pass.\n   - Passes 21 Dev unit tests and 16 new QA integration tests against real Postgres, including the NFR-1 concurrency guarantee.\n4. **The build is healthy, with no regressions.**\n   - `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` are both clean.\n   - `vitest run` shows 3 failing files. They are the same 3 failures recorded before this ticket (`DataTable` MUI X exports, `lockout` next-auth import, `useToast` timer), and none of them touch SH-6 code.\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (`enum PeriodKind`, `model Period`); migration 20261105000000_timetable; used by tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts |\n| FR-2 | PASS | `model SchoolDay` + migration; integration \"FR-7/FR-40\" test upserts and reads it |\n| FR-3 | PASS | `model TimetableSlot` with `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` and `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` in migration.sql; course FK `ON DELETE CASCADE` |\n| FR-4 | PASS | One additive migration with no ALTERs to existing tables except new FKs; back-relations on Course, Period and Room (schema lines 219/280/418/459); `prisma migrate status` reports it as up to date |\n| FR-5 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` and `BellScheduleEditor.tsx` are missing. Only the API exists. |\n| FR-6 | PASS | src/lib/validators/timetable.ts (`hhmm`, `periodSchema`); service `assertNoOverlap`; tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts (periodsOverlap, periodSchema) |\n| FR-7 | FAIL | The backend works: `updateSchoolDays` cascade-deletes slots and returns the count (integration \"FR-7/FR-40\"). The ToggleButton editor and the confirmation dialog are missing. |\n| FR-8 | PASS | `deletePeriod` throws CONFLICT with `details.slotCount`; integration \"FR-8\" |\n| FR-9 | PASS | clash-rules.ts TEACHER rule; unit (main and co-teacher, both directions); integration \"FR-9/FR-10\" (exact message) and \"co-teacher clash\" |\n| FR-10 | PASS | ROOM rule; unit; integration exact message `Clash: QA6-R1 is used by QA6-MATH-7A on Monday, QA6-P1.` |\n| FR-11 | PASS | SECTION rule; unit; integration \"FR-11\" exact message |\n| FR-12 | PASS | `overlapByCours