eact.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.\n- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:\n  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).\n  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.\n  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.\n  - Audit and notifications run after commit.\n- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).\n- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.\n- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.\n- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.\n- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:\n  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.\n  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).\n  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.\n  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.\n- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).\n  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.\n  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.\n  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".\n  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.\n  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)\n1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.\n2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:\n   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.\n   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.\n\n# QA Report — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-7\n- timestamp: 2026-11-06T12:35:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 51\n- requirementsPassed: 38\n- requirementsFailed: 13\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 QA report.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **BLOCKER (dependency issue from before SH-7): every attendance page that uses DataGrid fails to compile, so 9 FRs don't work in the running app.**\n   - Root cause: `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`. The lockfile resolves `@mui/x-internals` to `9.15.0` (because x-data-grid allows `^9.1.0`), and 9.15.0 no longer exports that path.\n   - QA reproduced it two ways:\n     - `node -e \"import('@mui/x-data-grid')\"` fails with *\"Package subpath './useFirstRender' is not defined by exports\"*.\n     - `next dev` logs `⨯ ./node_modules/@mui/x-data-grid/DataGrid/useDataGridComponent.mjs`.\n   - Pages that fail:\n     - `/students/[id]/attendance` (StudentAttendanceClient → DataTable).\n     - `/courses/[id]/attendance` (CourseAttendanceMatrix).\n     - **all of** `/admin/attendance`, because AdminAttendanceClient imports ReportTab statically, and ReportTab imports DataGrid. That takes down the Settings, Today and Below-threshold tabs as well.\n   - The **service and API layer behind these pages is proven correct** by the integration tests below. Each FAIL verdict blocked by this issue says so.\n   - Fix (a dependency change, outside SH-7's file ownership): pin `@mui/x-internals` to a version that matches 9.5, or upgrade all `@mui/x-*` packages together.\n2. **FAIL FR-22: an absent → present → absent sequence sends a second absence notification for the same session.**\n   - `notificationsFor` only compares against the previous save. Re-saving with no change is handled correctly, but the PRD says *\"Do not send more than one absence notification per student per session.\"*\n   - Evidence: `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts` › FR-22 (expected 1, got 2).\n   - Fix: inside the transaction, check for an existing `attendance.absent` notification for this student and session (or keep a per-record `absenceNotifiedAt`) before sending.\n3. **FAIL FR-19 (from the FR-10 check): once an admin marks any student EXCUSED, the teacher can no longer save that register.**\n   - `saveRegister` rejects any EXCUSED value in the body for non-admins (`attendance-service.ts:219`), even when the row is unchanged.\n   - The UI always sends the full roster, so a teacher's later correction to *another* student fails with 403. That breaks the teacher's 14-day edit right.\n   - Evidence: `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts` › FR-10/FR-19 (got FORBIDDEN).\n   - Fix: reject only rows whose status is EXCUSED **and** differs from the saved value. Do the check on `diff` inside the transaction.\n4. **FAIL NFR-10: `npm run test` cannot start** (issue from before SH-7). `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve. Every test in this report was run with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, the same config with the `vitest/config` import.\n5. **Carried over: the CSP still blocks hydration** (`next.config.js` `script-src 'self'`). The e2e only works with `bypassCSP: true`. See SH-1 QA blocker 1.\n\n## Test execution\n\n| Suite | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Typecheck | `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| Lint | `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings/errors |\n| `npm run test` | — | **does not start** (finding 4) |\n| Full vitest | `TEST_DATABASE_URL=… npx vitest run -c vitest.tmp.config.ts` | 225/229 pass. Failures: 2 QA SH-7 defect tests, plus 2 older failures (`auth-forms`, `useToast`). 2 older files fail to load (`DataTable`, `lockout`). |\n| SH-7 unit | attendance-rules (13) + attendance-register-form (8, new) | 21/21 pass |\n| SH-7 integration | attendance-service (7) + attendance-qa (10, new) | 15/17 pass (FR-22 and FR-19 fail) |\n| E2E | `APP_URL=http://localhost:3100 npx playwright test tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts` (next dev :3100) | teacher test ✓. Parent test: notification ✓ (2nd, warm run); calendar ✘ (page fails to compile) |\n| NFR-1 timing (local) | attendance-qa › NFR-1 | 35-student save **39–101 ms** (<500). 1,200-record tab **45–50 ms** (<400). |\n\nStatic checks:\n- No banned or non-MUI UI libraries are imported in any SH-7 file. The only third-party imports are `@prisma/client`, `date-fns(-tz)`, `next/*`, `react` and `zod`, plus `@mui/*`.\n- No `console.*` calls in SH-7 `src/` files.\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma; migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql:2,12-47 (enum, models, `sessionId_studentId` unique, `studentId_createdAt` index) |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0186m3yG3QxUBDAvXg5h2Zx3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
