{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmDaZPFFz72kp7pq9T5i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N4XyafCqVURGygqgknhBP8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/ui-verification/ui-verification-report.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:55:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"method\": \"`next dev -p 3300` against the local Postgres (:5433). The existing :3000 server was stale, returned 500 for every route, and belongs to another checkout, so it was left alone. The dev DB has no courses, sections or periods, so a throwaway Playwright driver (outside the repo) created tagged fixtures: teacher Terry Teach as course teacher and homeroom teacher, 3 students (Alex Absent, Lee Late, Pat Present), parent Paula linked to Alex, a 00:00–23:59 period, section 'uiv-att' with members, course 'UIV Attendance' enrolled 30 days back, and timetable slots on every weekday. attendanceMode was set to BOTH for the run and restored to PER_PERIOD. All fixtures were deleted afterwards (verified 0 rows). Viewports: 360×740 (teacher), 375×667 (parent), 1280×800 (desktop and admin). One pass ran with the shipped CSP enforced; the rest used bypassCSP:true, the same as QA and the e2e spec. Screenshots are in artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/ and raw probe output is in artifacts/ui-verification/uiv-raw.json. There is no figma-readiness.json, so the checks are against the PRD and requirements.json text only. Note: the first DataGrid compile failure leaves `next dev` returning 500 for every later request, so DataGrid pages were visited last.\",\n  \"blockingIssues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\n      \"summary\": \"MUI X version skew: @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0 imports @mui/x-internals/useFirstRender, but the installed x-internals 9.15.0 no longer exports it. Every SH-7 page with a DataGrid fails to compile.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Observed build-error overlays: /students/[id]/attendance (StudentAttendanceClient → DataTable), /admin/attendance (AdminAttendanceClient → ReportTab), and /courses/[courseId]/attendance (CourseAttendanceMatrix, seen in run 1 with a server-log import trace and a 500). The admin Settings, Today and Below-threshold tabs are lost as well, because ReportTab is a static import. This is the same root cause as QA finding 1, and it is outside SH-7 file ownership. Fix: pin @mui/x-internals to the 9.5 line or upgrade all @mui/x-* packages together.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\n      \"summary\": \"The shipped CSP (`script-src 'self'`) blocks hydration. With CSP enforced, the register never hydrates: 'Mark all present' does nothing and there are 10 CSP console errors.\",\n      \"detail\": \"This was present before SH-7 (QA finding 5 / SH-1 UIV-1). Screenshot: csp-register-360.png. The server-rendered markup is correct, but no client interaction works in a real browser.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance → Settings tab (attendanceMode, alert threshold)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"The page renders a Next 'Failed to compile' overlay (UIV-1). The import trace runs through ReportTab.tsx, so the Settings tab cannot be reached. Screenshot: admin-attendance-1280.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take landing (today's schedule)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"The content is correct: each meeting shows 'UIV Attendance – uiv-att · 00:00–23:59 · Now' with a 'Not taken' chip, and after the save it shows 'Taken 01:39 by Terry Teach' and a REVIEW button. Layout defect: at 360 px the page is 407 px wide. The 'Register date' DatePicker runs past the right edge, and the app bar stops at 360. Cause: PageHeader puts `actions` in a non-wrapping `Stack direction=\\\"row\\\"`, and DateNav's DatePicker keeps its full width beside the title. Screenshots: teacher-landing-360.png, teacher-landing-after-save-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take — 'Daily register – <section>' entry\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"With attendanceMode=BOTH, the homeroom teacher sees 'Daily register – uiv-att' with 'Not taken' and TAKE ATTENDANCE above the course meeting. Screenshot: teacher-landing-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register date picker and date limits\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The DatePicker renders (its 360 px overflow is reported under FR-6). A future date (2026-11-08) shows the alert 'Registers cannot be taken for future dates'. For the teacher, a 20-day-old date shows 'Teachers can edit registers up to 14 days after the register date'. An admin can open the same 20-day-old date. Screenshots: teacher-register-future-360.png, teacher-register-old-360.png, admin-register-1280.png. The calendar's own disabled-date UI was not clicked through.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/[courseId] register list\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Students are sorted by last name (Absent, Late, Present). Each row has an initials avatar, the name and an exclusive P/A/L/E ToggleButtonGroup with aria-labels ('Mark Alex Absent absent'). Nothing is preselected (Unmarked 3). Selected buttons use theme colours: A error-red, L warning-orange, P success-green. Screenshots: teacher-register-empty-360.png, teacher-register-saved-1280.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"surface\": \"EXCUSED (E) toggle\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"E is disabled (greyed) for the teacher and enabled for the admin.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"surface\": \"'Mark all present' button\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Lee was marked Absent first. 'Mark all present' then gave Present 2 · Absent 1, so it does not overwrite existing selections. The button is disabled once nobody is unmarked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"surface\": \"Minutes-late input and note field\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Selecting L reveals 'Minutes late' prefilled with 5. The note icon toggles a 'Note' text field; 'Called in sick' was entered and was still there after the save. The 1–240 range and the 500-character limit were not driven through the UI; the validators cover them and are unit-tested.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"surface\": \"Header counters and Save state\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The chips 'Present n · Absent n · Late n · Unmarked n' update live. Save is disabled while the bar reads '3 students not marked', and enabled once it reads 'Everyone is marked'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"surface\": \"Save and 'last changed' display\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The 'Attendance saved' toast appears, and 'Last changed by Terry Teach at 11/6/2026, 11:39:36 AM' shows on the saved register. Minor: this timestamp uses the browser's timezone (`toLocaleString`), while the landing page ('Taken 01:39') and the notification ('1:39 AM') use the school timezone (America/New_York). The same save therefore shows two different times. Screenshot: teacher-register-saved-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"surface\": \"Daily register roster\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The homeroom teacher's daily register lists the 3 section members (Unmarked 3). Screenshot: teacher-daily-register-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"This route reuses the register component, with the breadcrumb 'Take attendance / Daily register' and the title 'Daily register – uiv-att · Friday 6 Nov 2026'. Saving a daily register was not exercised in the UI; the integration tests cover it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register at 360 px\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"No horizontal overflow on the register page. Row heights are 110–158 px (at least 48). All 12 P/A/L/E toggles measure at least 44×49 px. The save bar is a Paper with position: sticky and bottom: 0, and it stays on screen over the rows (teacher-register-filled-360.png). The 360 px overflow on the landing page is reported under FR-6.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register past the 14-day window (teacher)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"PRD FR-4.2 and AC-4 say: 'Given a register date 20 days ago, when Tom opens it, then it is read-only with the explanation'. What renders is only the heading 'Register' and a warning alert; no roster, statuses or counters are shown. Cause: `canOpen` (FR-8 window) refuses the page before `canEdit`'s readOnly path can run. RegisterForm's read-only branch exists but teachers can never reach it. The admin can still edit at 20 days. Screenshot: teacher-register-old-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"surface\": \"Parent /notifications (absence notification)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"After the teacher marked Alex absent, parent Paula at 375 px sees 'Alex Absent was marked absent — UIV Attendance – uiv-att, uiv-att, Friday 6 Nov 2026' with an unread badge of 1. Screenshot: parent-notifications-375.png. FR-22 ('attendance.corrected') has no separate UI surface and was not exercised; QA found a duplicate-notification defect in the service layer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student 'Attendance' tab\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"/students/[id]/attendance returns 500 with the compile overlay (UIV-1). Screenshot: parent-student-attendance-375.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: summary cards\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render because the page fails to compile (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: month calendar (coloured days and tooltip)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). So the parent red-day check (AC / FR-41) cannot be verified visually.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: records table and note visibility\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). The DataTable itself is the failing import.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"surface\": \"/courses/[courseId]/attendance matrix\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run 1: GET returned 500 with 'Module not found: ./useFirstRender' and an import trace through CourseAttendanceMatrix.tsx. Not re-shot in run 2, because the dev server stays broken after the first DataGrid failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"The whole page fails to compile (UIV-1); see the FR-5 screenshot.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Missing registers and 'Remind teacher'\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance report builder and CSV\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). ReportTab is the module that triggers the failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Below threshold\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Teacher sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /attendance/take. Admin sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /admin/attendance in the main group (above 'Administration'). Screenshots: teacher-register-saved-1280.png, admin-dashboard-1280.png.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": { \"PASS\": 14, \"FAIL\": 6, \"BLOCKED\": 7 },\n  \"blockedReason\": null\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2110,"cache_read_input_tokens":90897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2110},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0d33c40-44ea-44a6-8793-0fcbf67c071f","uuid":"4188eddf-a3f3-4a5d-ad7d-8687c232c736","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:41:38.620Z","request_id":"req_011CgmDaZ8rzEF27QvyuG8iT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01N4XyafCqVURGygqgknhBP8":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/ui-verification/ui-verification-report.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:55:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"method\": \"`next dev -p 3300` against the local Postgres (:5433). The existing :3000 server was stale, returned 500 for every route, and belongs to another checkout, so it was left alone. The dev DB has no courses, sections or periods, so a throwaway Playwright driver (outside the repo) created tagged fixtures: teacher Terry Teach as course teacher and homeroom teacher, 3 students (Alex Absent, Lee Late, Pat Present), parent Paula linked to Alex, a 00:00–23:59 period, section 'uiv-att' with members, course 'UIV Attendance' enrolled 30 days back, and timetable slots on every weekday. attendanceMode was set to BOTH for the run and restored to PER_PERIOD. All fixtures were deleted afterwards (verified 0 rows). Viewports: 360×740 (teacher), 375×667 (parent), 1280×800 (desktop and admin). One pass ran with the shipped CSP enforced; the rest used bypassCSP:true, the same as QA and the e2e spec. Screenshots are in artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/ and raw probe output is in artifacts/ui-verification/uiv-raw.json. There is no figma-readiness.json, so the checks are against the PRD and requirements.json text only. Note: the first DataGrid compile failure leaves `next dev` returning 500 for every later request, so DataGrid pages were visited last.\",\n  \"blockingIssues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\n      \"summary\": \"MUI X version skew: @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0 imports @mui/x-internals/useFirstRender, but the installed x-internals 9.15.0 no longer exports it. Every SH-7 page with a DataGrid fails to compile.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Observed build-error overlays: /students/[id]/attendance (StudentAttendanceClient → DataTable), /admin/attendance (AdminAttendanceClient → ReportTab), and /courses/[courseId]/attendance (CourseAttendanceMatrix, seen in run 1 with a server-log import trace and a 500). The admin Settings, Today and Below-threshold tabs are lost as well, because ReportTab is a static import. This is the same root cause as QA finding 1, and it is outside SH-7 file ownership. Fix: pin @mui/x-internals to the 9.5 line or upgrade all @mui/x-* packages together.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\n      \"summary\": \"The shipped CSP (`script-src 'self'`) blocks hydration. With CSP enforced, the register never hydrates: 'Mark all present' does nothing and there are 10 CSP console errors.\",\n      \"detail\": \"This was present before SH-7 (QA finding 5 / SH-1 UIV-1). Screenshot: csp-register-360.png. The server-rendered markup is correct, but no client interaction works in a real browser.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance → Settings tab (attendanceMode, alert threshold)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"The page renders a Next 'Failed to compile' overlay (UIV-1). The import trace runs through ReportTab.tsx, so the Settings tab cannot be reached. Screenshot: admin-attendance-1280.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take landing (today's schedule)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"The content is correct: each meeting shows 'UIV Attendance – uiv-att · 00:00–23:59 · Now' with a 'Not taken' chip, and after the save it shows 'Taken 01:39 by Terry Teach' and a REVIEW button. Layout defect: at 360 px the page is 407 px wide. The 'Register date' DatePicker runs past the right edge, and the app bar stops at 360. Cause: PageHeader puts `actions` in a non-wrapping `Stack direction=\\\"row\\\"`, and DateNav's DatePicker keeps its full width beside the title. Screenshots: teacher-landing-360.png, teacher-landing-after-save-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take — 'Daily register – <section>' entry\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"With attendanceMode=BOTH, the homeroom teacher sees 'Daily register – uiv-att' with 'Not taken' and TAKE ATTENDANCE above the course meeting. Screenshot: teacher-landing-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register date picker and date limits\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The DatePicker renders (its 360 px overflow is reported under FR-6). A future date (2026-11-08) shows the alert 'Registers cannot be taken for future dates'. For the teacher, a 20-day-old date shows 'Teachers can edit registers up to 14 days after the register date'. An admin can open the same 20-day-old date. Screenshots: teacher-register-future-360.png, teacher-register-old-360.png, admin-register-1280.png. The calendar's own disabled-date UI was not clicked through.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/[courseId] register list\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Students are sorted by last name (Absent, Late, Present). Each row has an initials avatar, the name and an exclusive P/A/L/E ToggleButtonGroup with aria-labels ('Mark Alex Absent absent'). Nothing is preselected (Unmarked 3). Selected buttons use theme colours: A error-red, L warning-orange, P success-green. Screenshots: teacher-register-empty-360.png, teacher-register-saved-1280.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"surface\": \"EXCUSED (E) toggle\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"E is disabled (greyed) for the teacher and enabled for the admin.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"surface\": \"'Mark all present' button\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Lee was marked Absent first. 'Mark all present' then gave Present 2 · Absent 1, so it does not overwrite existing selections. The button is disabled once nobody is unmarked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"surface\": \"Minutes-late input and note field\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Selecting L reveals 'Minutes late' prefilled with 5. The note icon toggles a 'Note' text field; 'Called in sick' was entered and was still there after the save. The 1–240 range and the 500-character limit were not driven through the UI; the validators cover them and are unit-tested.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"surface\": \"Header counters and Save state\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The chips 'Present n · Absent n · Late n · Unmarked n' update live. Save is disabled while the bar reads '3 students not marked', and enabled once it reads 'Everyone is marked'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"surface\": \"Save and 'last changed' display\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The 'Attendance saved' toast appears, and 'Last changed by Terry Teach at 11/6/2026, 11:39:36 AM' shows on the saved register. Minor: this timestamp uses the browser's timezone (`toLocaleString`), while the landing page ('Taken 01:39') and the notification ('1:39 AM') use the school timezone (America/New_York). The same save therefore shows two different times. Screenshot: teacher-register-saved-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"surface\": \"Daily register roster\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The homeroom teacher's daily register lists the 3 section members (Unmarked 3). Screenshot: teacher-daily-register-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"This route reuses the register component, with the breadcrumb 'Take attendance / Daily register' and the title 'Daily register – uiv-att · Friday 6 Nov 2026'. Saving a daily register was not exercised in the UI; the integration tests cover it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register at 360 px\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"No horizontal overflow on the register page. Row heights are 110–158 px (at least 48). All 12 P/A/L/E toggles measure at least 44×49 px. The save bar is a Paper with position: sticky and bottom: 0, and it stays on screen over the rows (teacher-register-filled-360.png). The 360 px overflow on the landing page is reported under FR-6.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register past the 14-day window (teacher)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"PRD FR-4.2 and AC-4 say: 'Given a register date 20 days ago, when Tom opens it, then it is read-only with the explanation'. What renders is only the heading 'Register' and a warning alert; no roster, statuses or counters are shown. Cause: `canOpen` (FR-8 window) refuses the page before `canEdit`'s readOnly path can run. RegisterForm's read-only branch exists but teachers can never reach it. The admin can still edit at 20 days. Screenshot: teacher-register-old-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"surface\": \"Parent /notifications (absence notification)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"After the teacher marked Alex absent, parent Paula at 375 px sees 'Alex Absent was marked absent — UIV Attendance – uiv-att, uiv-att, Friday 6 Nov 2026' with an unread badge of 1. Screenshot: parent-notifications-375.png. FR-22 ('attendance.corrected') has no separate UI surface and was not exercised; QA found a duplicate-notification defect in the service layer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student 'Attendance' tab\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"/students/[id]/attendance returns 500 with the compile overlay (UIV-1). Screenshot: parent-student-attendance-375.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: summary cards\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render because the page fails to compile (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: month calendar (coloured days and tooltip)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). So the parent red-day check (AC / FR-41) cannot be verified visually.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: records table and note visibility\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). The DataTable itself is the failing import.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"surface\": \"/courses/[courseId]/attendance matrix\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run 1: GET returned 500 with 'Module not found: ./useFirstRender' and an import trace through CourseAttendanceMatrix.tsx. Not re-shot in run 2, because the dev server stays broken after the first DataGrid failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"The whole page fails to compile (UIV-1); see the FR-5 screenshot.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Missing registers and 'Remind teacher'\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance report builder and CSV\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). ReportTab is the module that triggers the failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Below threshold\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Teacher sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /attendance/take. Admin sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /admin/attendance in the main group (above 'Administration'). Screenshots: teacher-register