{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ExZmGDapjaRYBgSz1QN6pi","type":"tool_result","content":"# Dev Log — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)\n\n> The previous content of this file was a stale SH-4 log. Per the dev-planning note\n> (\"Stale SH-1 artifacts under artifacts/dev/ must be regenerated, not reused\") it was\n> replaced. This is SH-7's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-06)\n\nAll 19 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 36 owned files exist.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma schema + attendance migration (CHECK + 2 partial unique indexes) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Zod validators (src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: 4 attendance notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Settings input + PATCH /api/settings/school — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Pure rules module + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: getSchoolScheduleForDate in the timetable service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: Attendance service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: Integration tests (attendance-service) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: Teacher API routes (today, register GET/PUT) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: Student/course attendance API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Admin API routes (overview, report+CSV, below-threshold, remind) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: RegisterForm client component — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Take pages + DateNav — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: Student Attendance tab — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: Course Attendance tab (matrix) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Admin attendance page (Today / Report / Below threshold / Settings) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: Tab + navigation config entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Seed attendance (mulberry32, idempotent) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Playwright e2e at 375×667 — ✓ complete (file written and run; see verification for which assertions were proven)\n\n### Implementation notes\n- **Migration (TASK-1).** Generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel`, the equivalent of `--create-only` with no shadow DB. The diff is additive only. The CHECK constraint and the two partial unique indexes were then appended by hand. Applied to the local DB with `migrate deploy`.\n- **Service, outside Next (TASK-7).** The service does not import `services/settings.ts`, because its `react.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.\n- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:\n  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).\n  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.\n  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.\n  - Audit and notifications run after commit.\n- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).\n- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.\n- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.\n- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.\n- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:\n  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.\n  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).\n  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.\n  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.\n- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).\n  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.\n  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.\n  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".\n  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.\n  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)\n1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.\n2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:\n   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.\n   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.\n   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.\n   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.\n3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.\n4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.\n5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.\n6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100.\n# QA Report — SH-8 (PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-8\n- timestamp: 2026-11-07T03:45:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 60\n- requirementsPassed: 21\n- requirementsFailed: 39\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 QA report. Of the 39 failed requirements, 2 are FAIL and 37 are NOT-IMPLEMENTED.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n### 1. BLOCKER: the Dev phase for SH-8 is incomplete, and it left no report\n\n- `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `artifacts/dev/task-completion-markers.json` are still the **SH-7** files. Dev never wrote SH-8 versions.\n- `dev-rerun-count.json` shows `count: 3, firstPassAccepted: false`.\n- `security-scan-report.json` (SH-8) scanned **0 files**.\n- QA therefore checked reality against `file-ownership-matrix.json` (SH-8) directly. **33 of the 66 owned paths are missing on disk.**\n\n### 2. What was built: the file storage backend (TASK-1 to TASK-8, roughly)\n\n- Built:\n  - dependencies, env vars and `.gitignore`\n  - the Prisma models and migration\n  - `storage.ts`\n  - upload validation\n  - the visibility rule and video parser\n  - the access registry and built-in contexts\n  - the files service\n  - the `/api/files` routes\n  - the orphan purge and its maintenance hook\n  - the content Zod validators\n- This code is real (no stubs or TODOs). It typechecks and lints clean, and it passes 40/40 tests, including the 14 QA added.\n\n### 3. What is missing: TASK-10 to TASK-21\n\n- **Server:** the content service, every content/lesson/module/progress/learning API route, and the settings validator.\n- **UI:** every UI component (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, StatusChip, VideoEmbed) and every page (Content tab, lesson viewer and editor, Learning tab, `/admin/settings/school`).\n- **Seed:** the seed content and the seed PDF asset.\n- **Tests:** the Dev-owned integration, Markdown and e2e tests.\n- **Effect:** no course-content feature is usable by any role.\n\n### 4. Pre-existing: `npm test` does not start\n\n- `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js` (MODULE_NOT_FOUND). This was carried over from SH-7 and is not caused by SH-8.\n- All runs used `vitest.tmp.config.ts`.\n\n### 5. Minor (not a defect)\n\n- If an uploaded filename contains a raw control character in the multipart header, busboy rejects it as \"Malformed multipart body\" before `sanitizeFilename` runs.\n- That is a safe failure. Browsers do not send raw control characters.\n- `sanitizeFilename` itself strips them (unit-tested).\n\n## Commands run\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | exit 0 |\n| `npx eslint` on all SH-8 source and test files | exit 0 |\n| `npx prisma migrate status` | 9 migrations, DB up to date (the SH-8 migration is applied) |\n| `npx vitest run --config vitest.tmp.config.ts` on the 5 SH-8 unit tests | 30/30 pass |\n| `TEST_DATABASE_URL=… npx vitest run --config vitest.tmp.config.ts tests/integration/files-qa.test.ts` | 10/10 pass |\n| `npx vitest run` (`npm test`) | fails to start (pre-existing config break) |\n\n## Tests added by QA\n\n- **tests/integration/files-qa.test.ts** (10 tests, real Postgres plus a temp UPLOAD_DIR). It covers:\n  - PNG upload with sha256, key format, server-side MIME and path under UPLOAD_DIR\n  - rejection of .exe, an ELF disguised as .txt, SVG outside logo, and oversize files\n  - txt and logo-SVG accepted\n  - owner/admin can download an unattached file; others and anonymous get NOT_FOUND\n  - an attached logo is public; a lesson file pointing at a missing lesson is denied\n  - attaching someone else's file is refused\n  - delete: owner OK (row and bytes), attached → CONFLICT, stranger → NOT_FOUND\n  - an admin delete writes an audit row\n  - 61st upload → RATE_LIMITED\n  - orphan purge: only unattached files older than 24 h, with their bytes\n- **tests/unit/content-validators.test.ts** (4 tests). It covers:\n  - FR-16 field limits\n  - link and video URL rules\n  - SCHEDULED must be in the future\n  - the reorder schema shape\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma:564 FileObject (unique storageKey, @@index [context, contextId]); migration 20261108000000 applied; files-qa writes and reads rows |\n| FR-2 | PASS | src/server/storage.ts (saveFile/readFile/deleteFile, traversal guard); UPLOAD_DIR in env.ts and .env.example; `uploads/` in .gitignore; files-qa asserts the path is under UPLOAD_DIR |\n| FR-3 | PASS | src/app/api/files/route.ts → uploadFile; files-qa \"stores a valid PNG unattached\" (contextId null) |\n| FR-4 | PASS | files-service.ts mid-stream cap; files-qa asserts \"File exceeds 1 MB.\" (MAX_UPLOAD_MB=1) |\n| FR-5 | PASS | validate.ts ALLOWED + file-type sniff; file-validate.test.ts; files-qa \".exe is not allowed\" |\n| FR-6 | PASS | validate.ts sniff modes; file-validate.test.ts (OOXML-as-zip, txt with no signature); files-qa ELF-as-.txt rejected |\n| FR-7 | PASS | validate.ts sanitizeFilename; file-validate.test.ts (separators, control chars, 150 cap); files-qa |\n| FR-8 | PASS | src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts sets the stored MIME, nosniff, attachment, and inline only for image/pdf with ?inline=1 (code-reviewed; no route-level test, see coverage-report) |\n| FR-9 | PASS | src/server/files/access.ts; file-access.test.ts (dispatch, unknown context → owner/admin, resolver throw → deny); files-qa NOT_FOUND before streaming |\n| FR-10 | PASS | src/server/files/contexts.ts lesson + logo resolvers; files-qa: anonymous can fetch an attached logo, a lesson file for a missing lesson is denied |\n| FR-11 | PASS | files-service.ts deleteUnattachedFile; files-qa delete (row and bytes gone, attached → CONFLICT, stranger → NOT_FOUND) |\n| FR-12 | PASS | src/server/files/purge.ts; called in api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts:38; files-qa purge test |\n| FR-13 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx missing |\n| FR-14 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx missing |\n| FR-15 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma:581-650: ContentStatus, Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink, LessonProgress (cascades, @@id [lessonId, studentId]); `prisma migrate status` up to date |\n| FR-16 | PASS | src/lib/validators/content.ts; tests/unit/content-validators.test.ts |\n| FR-17 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The attachFiles helper works (files-qa), but no lesson flow calls it: the PATCH /api/lessons/:id route and content-service.ts are missing |\n| FR-18 | PASS | src/server/content/visibility.ts isLessonVisible (read-time, pure); visibility.test.ts. Also used by contexts.ts. The list/get consumers are missing (see FR-43/44) |\n| FR-19 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | canSeeDrafts exists, but the status badge (content/StatusChip.tsx) and the Content tab are missing |\n| FR-20 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | Content tab page/ContentOutline missing; no 'content' entry in src/config/course-tabs.ts |\n| FR-21 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No progress UI (ContentOutline missing) |\n| FR-22 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No teacher controls (ContentOutline missing) |\n| FR-23 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | reorderSchema exists, but api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts and the dnd UI are missing |\n| FR-24 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No module delete flow (UI and api/modules/[id] missing) |\n| FR-25 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx and LessonEditor.tsx missing |\n| FR-26 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | LessonEditor.tsx missing |\n| FR-27 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | LessonEditor.tsx and api/lessons/[id] missing |\n| FR-28 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The schedule-in-future validator passes (content-validators.test.ts), but there are no status controls or picker (LessonEditor missing) |\n| FR-29 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No autosave (LessonEditor missing) |\n| FR-30 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The parser and embedUrl pass (video.test.ts), but the embed renderer content/VideoEmbed.tsx is missing |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4236bb9b-3e91-459f-a600-1de35f9962e2","uuid":"4bc8a16e-80b7-42b7-a219-4c494f02bd70","timestamp":"2026-11-07T04:07:45.347Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Dev Log — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)\n\n> The previous content of this file was a stale SH-4 log. Per the dev-planning note\n> (\"Stale SH-1 artifacts under artifacts/dev/ must be regenerated, not reused\") it was\n> replaced. This is SH-7's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-06)\n\nAll 19 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 36 owned files exist.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma schema + attendance migration (CHECK + 2 partial unique indexes) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Zod validators (src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: 4 attendance notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Settings input + PATCH /api/settings/school — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Pure rules module + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: getSchoolScheduleForDate in the timetable service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: Attendance service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: Integration tests (attendance-service) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: Teacher API routes (today, register GET/PUT) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: Student/course attendance API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Admin API routes (overview, report+CSV, below-threshold, remind) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: RegisterForm client component — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Take pages + DateNav — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: Student Attendance tab — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: Course Attendance tab (matrix) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Admin attendance page (Today / Report / Below threshold / Settings) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: Tab + navigation config entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Seed attendance (mulberry32, idempotent) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Playwright e2e at 375×667 — ✓ complete (file written and run; see verification for which assertions were proven)\n\n### Implementation notes\n- **Migration (TASK-1).** Generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel`, the equivalent of `--create-only` with no shadow DB. The diff is additive only. The CHECK constraint and the two partial unique indexes were then appended by hand. Applied to the local DB with `migrate deploy`.\n- **Service, outside Next (TASK-7).** The service does not import `services/settings.ts`, because its `react.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.\n- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:\n  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).\n  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.\n  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.\n  - Audit and notifications run after commit.\n- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).\n- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.\n- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.\n- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.\n- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:\n  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.\n  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).\n  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.\n  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.\n- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).\n  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.\n  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.\n  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".\n  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.\n  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)\n1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.\n2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:\n   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.\n   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.\n   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.\n   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.\n3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.\n4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.\n5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.\n6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100.\n# QA Report — SH-8 (PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-8\n- timestamp: 2026-11-07T03:45:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 60\n- requirementsPassed: 21\n- requirementsFailed: 39\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 QA report. Of the 39 failed requirements, 2 are FAIL and 37 are NOT-IMPLEMENTED.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n### 1. BLOCKER: the Dev phase for SH-8 is incomplete, and it left no report\n\n- `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `artifacts/dev/task-completion-markers.json` are still the **SH-7** files. Dev never wrote SH-8 versions.\n- `dev-rerun-count.json` shows `count: 3, firstPassAccepted: false`.\n- `security-scan-report.json` (SH-8) scanned **0 files**.\n- QA therefore checked reality against `file-ownership-matrix.json` (SH-8) directly. **33 of the 66 owned paths are missing on disk.**\n\n### 2. What was built: the file storage backend (TASK-1 to TASK-8, roughly)\n\n- Built:\n  - dependencies, env vars and `.gitignore`\n  - the Prisma models and migration\n  - `storage.ts`\n  - upload validation\n  - the visibility rule and video parser\n  - the access registry and built-in contexts\n  - the files service\n  - the `/api/files` routes\n  - the orphan purge and its maintenance hook\n  - the content Zod validators\n- This code is real (no stubs or TODOs). It typechecks and lints clean, and it passes 40/40 tests, including the 14 QA added.\n\n### 3. What is missing: TASK-10 to TASK-21\n\n- **Server:** the content service, every content/lesson/module/progress/learning API route, and the settings validator.\n- **UI:** every UI component (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, StatusChip, VideoEmbed) and every page (Content tab, lesson viewer and editor, Learning tab, `/admin/settings/school`).\n- **Seed:** the seed content and the seed PDF asset.\n- **Tests:** the Dev-owned integration, Markdown and e2e tests.\n- **Effect:** no course-content feature is usable by any role.\n\n### 4. Pre-existing: `npm test` does not start\n\n- `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js` (MODULE_NOT_FOUND). This was carried over from SH-7 and is not caused by SH-8.\n- All runs used `vitest.tmp.config.ts`.\n\n### 5. Minor (not a defect)\n\n- If an uploaded filename contains a raw control character in the multipart header, busboy rejects it as \"Malformed multipart body\" before `sanitizeFilename` runs.\n- That is a safe failure. Browsers do not send raw control characters.\n- `sanitizeFilename` itself strips them (unit-tested).\n\n## Commands run\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | exit 0 |\n| `npx eslint` on all SH-8 source and test files | exit 0 |\n| `npx prisma migrate status` | 9 migrations, DB up to date (the SH-8 migration is applied) |\n| `npx vitest run --config vitest.tmp.config.ts` on the 5 SH-8 unit tests | 30/30 pass |\n| `TEST_DATABASE_URL=… npx vitest run --config vitest.tmp.config.ts tests/integration/files-qa.test.ts` | 10/10 pass |\n| `npx vitest run` (`npm test`) | fails to start (pre-existing config break) |\n\n## Tests added by QA\n\n- **tests/integration/files-qa.test.ts** (10 tests, real Postgres plus a temp UPLOAD_DIR). It covers:\n  - PNG upload with sha256, key format, server-side MIME and path under UPLOAD_DIR\n  - rejection of .exe, an ELF disguised as .txt, SVG outside logo, and oversize files\n  - txt and logo-SVG accepted\n  - owner/admin can download an unattached file; others and anonymous get NOT_FOUND\n  - an attached logo is public; a lesson file pointing at a missing lesson is denied\n  - attaching someone else's file is refused\n  - delete: owner OK (row and bytes), attached → CONFLICT, stranger → NOT_FOUND\n  - an admin delete writes an audit row\n  - 61st upload → RATE_LIMITED\n  - orphan purge: only unattached files older than 24 h, with their bytes\n- **tests/unit/content-validators.test.ts** (4 tests). It covers:\n  - FR-16 field limits\n  - link and video URL rules\n  - SCHEDULED must be in the future\n  - the reorder schema shape\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma:564 FileObject (unique storageKey, @@index [context, contextId]); migration 20261108000000 applied; files-qa writes and reads rows |\n| FR-2 | PASS | src/server/storage.ts (saveFile/readFile/deleteFile, traversal guard); UPLOAD_DIR in env.ts and .env.example; `uploads/` in .gitignore; files-qa asserts the path is under UPLOAD_DIR |\n| FR-3 | PASS | src/app/api/files/route.ts → uploadFile; files-qa \"stores a valid PNG unattached\" (contextId null) |\n| FR-4 | PASS | files-service.ts mid-stream cap; files-qa asserts \"File exceeds 1 MB.\" (MAX_UPLOAD_MB=1) |\n| FR-5 | PASS | validate.ts ALLOWED + file-type sniff; file-validate.test.ts; files-qa \".exe is not allowed\" |\n| FR-6 | PASS | validate.ts sniff modes; file-validate.test.ts (OOXML-as-zip, txt with no signature); files-qa ELF-as-.txt rejected |\n| FR-7 | PASS | validate.ts sanitizeFilename; file-validate.test.ts (separators, control chars, 150 cap); files-qa |\n| FR-8 | PASS | src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts sets the stored MIME, nosniff, attachment, and inline only for image/pdf with ?inline=1 (code-reviewed; no route-level test, see coverage-report) |\n| FR-9 | PASS | src/server/files/access.ts; file-access.test.ts (dispatch, unknown context → owner/admin, resolver throw → deny); files-qa NOT_FOUND before streaming |\n| FR-10 | PASS | src/server/files/contexts.ts lesson + logo resolvers; files-qa: anonymous can fetch an attached logo, a lesson file for a missing lesson is denied |\n| FR-11 | PASS | files-service.ts deleteUnattachedFile; files-qa delete (row and bytes gone, attached → CONFLICT, stranger → NOT_FOUND) |\n| FR-12 | PASS | src/server/files/purge.ts; called in api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts:38; files-qa purge test |\n| FR-13 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx missing |\n| FR-14 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx missing |\n| FR-15 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma:581-650: ContentStatus, Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink, LessonProgress (cascades, @@id [lessonId, studentId]); `prisma migrate status` up to date |\n| FR-16 | PASS | src/lib/validators/content.ts; tests/unit/content-validators.test.ts |\n| FR-17 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The attachFiles helper works (files-qa), but no lesson flow calls it: the PATCH /api/lessons/:id route and content-service.ts are missing |\n| FR-18 | PASS | src/server/content/visibility.ts isLessonVisible (read-time, pure); visibility.test.ts. Also used by contexts.ts. The list/get consumers are missing (see FR-43/44) |\n| FR-19 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | canSeeDrafts exists, but the status badge (content/StatusChip.tsx) and the Content tab are missing |\n| FR-20 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | Content tab page/ContentOutline missing; no 'content' entry in src/config/course-tabs.ts |\n| FR-21 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No progress UI (ContentOutline missing) |\n| FR-22 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No teacher controls (ContentOutline missing) |\n| FR-23 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | reorderSchema exists, but api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts and the dnd UI are missing |\n| FR-24 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No module delete flow (UI and api/modules/[id] missing) |\n| FR-25 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx and LessonEditor.tsx missing |\n| FR-26 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | LessonEditor.tsx missing |\n| FR-27 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | LessonEditor.tsx and api/lessons/[id] missing |\n| FR-28 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The schedule-in-future validator passes (content-validators.test.ts), but there are no status controls or picker (LessonEditor missing) |\n| FR-29 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No autosave (LessonEditor missing) |\n| FR-30 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The parser and embedUrl pass (video.test.ts), but the embed renderer content/VideoEmbed.tsx is missing |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ExZmGDapjaRYBgSz1QN6pi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
