t dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)\n\nAll 26 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in\n`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 55 matrix paths were verified on disk (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is deleted as planned).\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Environment fixes (x-internals override, vitest import, delete tmp config) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Prisma schema + migration add_assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: grading-math.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: nextTeachingDayDueAt in src/lib/dates.ts + DST tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Publishable type widened + 4 notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: assignments-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: reminders.ts + dispatcher hook — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: assignment/submission file resolvers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: course/assignment/duplicate route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: submission/grading route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: /api/me/assignments + /api/students/[id]/assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: next.config.js header split (D11) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: MarkdownView + MarkdownEditor — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: FileUpload + FileList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: course-tabs / navigation / student-tabs entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: RubricBuilder — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: AssignmentForm + new/edit pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: AssignmentList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Course Assignments tab + CourseAssignmentsTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: Assignment page + SubmissionPanel — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: Grading page + GradingWorkspace — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: /assignments + /students/[id]/assignments pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: Idempotent FR-61 seed block — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: Integration tests (submissions, grading, reminders) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: Playwright e2e — ✓ complete\n\n### Verification run this iteration\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |\n| Unit: `tests/unit/assignments/*`, `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |\n| Integration: `tests/integration/assignments/*` (`TEST_DATABASE_URL` = local Postgres :5433, tagged fixtures, cleaned up) | 14 / 14 pass; 3 consecutive full-folder runs green |\n| `npm run build` | **passes** (needs network access for `next/font` Google Fonts) |\n| e2e `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` against a fresh `next start -p 3100` | 5 / 5 pass |\n| Seed: run twice against temporary MATH-7A/ELA-7A/SCI-7A courses | 7 created, then 0 (idempotent); missing courses skip with a log line. Temp data removed. |\n| Migration `20261109000000_add_assignments` | applied with `prisma migrate deploy`; additive only (no DROP/ALTER of existing tables) |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp gate | reachable. `useMuiDocs` (material-ui 9.5.0 llms.txt) + `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup and LinearProgress. Other components follow existing in-repo v9 usage. |\n\n### Decisions and deviations (for QA / reviewer)\n1. **ADR-2 is not enough on its own — follow-up fix in `next.config.js`.** With `@mui/x-internals` pinned to 9.1.0 (`npm ls` shows 9.1.0 everywhere), `next build` still failed with\n   `'useFirstRender' is not exported`. Root cause: webpack resolves `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender` to its **CJS** build. That build re-exports through `Object.keys`, which webpack can't analyse statically,\n   so x-data-grid's `export *` of it breaks. Fix: one `webpack()` alias that points that specifier at the ESM file (commented, removable on a MUI X upgrade). With the alias,\n   DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9) build, so **no D2 fallbacks were needed**. This touches `next.config.js`, which the plan gives to TASK-13. It's logged here as part of TASK-1's environment fix.\n   The pin is kept, because the alias targets the 9.1.0 file.\n2. **Decimal source:** `grading-math.ts` imports `Decimal` from `@prisma/client/runtime/index-browser.js`, which is Prisma's bundled decimal.js. The plain `decimal.js` package is only a transitive\n   **devDependency** (via jsdom), so it would be missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.\n3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    \"TASK-3\",\n    \"TASK-4\",\n    \"TASK-5\",\n    \"TASK-6\",\n    \"TASK-7\",\n    \"TASK-8\",\n    \"TASK-9\",\n    \"TASK-10\",\n    \"TASK-11\",\n    \"TASK-12\",\n    \"TASK-13\",\n    \"TASK-14\",\n    \"TASK-15\",\n    \"TASK-16\",\n    \"TASK-17\",\n    \"TASK-18\",\n    \"TASK-19\",\n    \"TASK-20\",\n    \"TASK-21\",\n    \"TASK-22\",\n    \"TASK-23\",\n    \"TASK-24\",\n    \"TASK-25\",\n    \"TASK-26\"\n  ]\n}\n# QA Report — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-9\n- timestamp: 2026-11-09T06:10:50Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 78\n- requirementsPassed: 76\n- requirementsFailed: 2\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-8 QA report. All 61 functional requirements PASS. The 2 failures are non-functional:\n> **NFR-12** is a small fix (3 `console.log` lines in the seed). **NFR-13** fails because `npm run test` is not fully green. All 6 failing tests are outside SH-9 and existed before it.\n> The feature is complete and works end to end. It is ready for review once NFR-12 is fixed and the NFR-13 failures are accepted as known or fixed separately.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n### 1. The build and test suite run, and the feature works end to end\n- `tsc --noEmit` is clean and `npm run lint` is clean.\n- All 57 SH-9 tests are green (29 unit, 23 integration against a real Postgres on :5433, 5 Playwright e2e against `next start -p 3100`).\n- QA added `tests/integration/assignments/qa-sh9.test.ts` (9 tests). It covers what Dev's tests did not: scheduling and visibility, publish-once, delete vs archive, duplicate, privacy and access control, the roster, \"To grade\", and editing max points.\n- All 9 pass. QA found no functional defects.\n- Dev's self-report checked out. All 55 `file-ownership-matrix.json` paths are present (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` was deleted as planned). A grep found no TODO, FIXME or stub implementations in the SH-9 files.\n\n### 2. NFR-13: `npm run test` is not fully green, and the cause is outside SH-9\nThe full suite passed 306 of 312 tests on the first run. The 6 failures:\n\n| Test | Failure | Why it is not SH-9 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `attendance-qa.test.ts` FR-22 | expected 2 absence notifications to be 1 | `attendance-service.ts` was last changed Nov 6, before SH-9. SH-9 only added entries to `notifications/types.ts`. |\n| `attendance-qa.test.ts` FR-10/FR-19 | `FORBIDDEN` vs `OK` | Depends on the time of day (the attendance edit window). Not SH-9 code. |\n| `attendance-qa.test.ts` NFR-1 perf | timing | Flaky: it passed on the rerun. |\n| `auth.test.ts` rate limit | — | Flaky: it passed on the rerun. |\n| `auth-forms.test.tsx`, `useToast.test.tsx` | focus and timer assertions | Do not import SH-9 code. |\n| `lockout.test.ts` | next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM | Environment problem. Not SH-9 code. |\n\n- The repo has no git baseline: the git root is `$HOME` and the whole project is untracked. Before SH-9, `vitest.config.ts` could not load at all.\n- So QA cannot prove these failures existed before SH-9. The evidence above (file dates, imports, flakiness) points that way.\n- Strictly, NFR-13 (\"npm run test keeps passing\") is **not met**. It needs a separate fix outside this ticket.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d5985c3-c3cf-4564-ae4d-e780109f626c","uuid":"5314a9c0-a9d6-400b-9d2d-d78839e77b40","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:12:45.910Z",