{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgs3SeRV4N2CcPVikiXCk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"UI verification for SH-10 is complete, with one failure: the quiz timer and title disappear under the app bar once a student scrolls down. 24 checks passed, 1 failed and none were blocked.\n\n**The failure (FR-14):** the quiz player's header is meant to stay pinned at the top, but it pins at the very top of the window, where the app bar already sits. After scrolling, the app bar covers the quiz title, the countdown timer and the save-status pill, on both phone (375px) and desktop (1280px) widths. On desktop it also covers the Submit button. I confirmed this by measuring element positions after a scroll and with screenshots (`student-player-scrolled-375.png`, `student-player-scrolled-1280.png`). The likely fix is a one-line change in `QuizPlayer.tsx`: push the pinned header down by the app bar's height (56px on phone, 64px on desktop). I didn't change any code.\n\n**How I checked:** I made a production build, ran it on port 3300, and drove it with a Playwright script kept in `/tmp/uiv-sh10/`, outside the repo. It used test users, a course and six quizzes, which I deleted afterwards. The full flow worked:\n- **Teacher:** created a quiz, added all five question types, duplicated and deleted a question, and used the student preview, which recorded nothing.\n- **Teacher:** the publish checklist blocks a quiz with an unanswered choice question, and editing locks once attempts exist.\n- **Student:** started a quiz and answered it. Autosave worked, including going offline and back. A page reload kept every answer, and submitting showed the unanswered count.\n- **Grading and results:** the teacher graded the essay and the attempt became fully graded. The student and parent result pages, the manual-release \"results will be available later\" state, the red timer under 2 minutes and analytics with the chart and CSV export all rendered correctly.\n- **No leaked answers:** the student's browser never received correct answers before results were released.\n\n**Smaller issues:**\n- **Analytics chart:** the accessibility scanner (axe) says the score chart has no text alternative, which it rates serious. It also flagged a heading-order issue.\n- **Teacher quiz table:** the actions column has no header label (minor).\n\n**Not exercised through the UI** (QA's automated tests cover these):\n- the error for a time limit longer than the quiz window\n- saving extra time or extra attempts for a student\n- Regrade and Release results\n- drag-to-reorder\n- image upload\n\nThere's no Figma reference (`figma-readiness.json` doesn't exist), so I compared against `requirements.json` only. The old SH-9 report and screenshots in that folder have been replaced. The Markdown report was written after the JSON one, and the test server is stopped.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/ui-verification/`:\n- `ui-verification-report.md`\n- `ui-verification-report.json`\n- `uiv-raw.json`\n- `screenshots/` (32 files)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1508,"cache_read_input_tokens":127643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1508,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ac7f625-80e7-44e9-9e39-f496ace1cf88","uuid":"c1417727-afc9-4f45-a9cb-ca4ce3d92978","timestamp":"2026-11-09T08:31:47.387Z","request_id":"req_011Cgs3SeDLKoiNjTVyc6nhG"}
